
<section class="page-content">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2>The ritual of burning</h2>
      <p>A candle is only as good as how you burn it. Follow these guidelines and your candle will give you 45–80 hours of clean, even scent — and a vessel that lives on.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="care-steps stagger">
      <div class="care-step">
        <div class="care-step-num">01</div>
        <h4>Trim the wick</h4>
        <p>Before every burn, trim the cotton wick to 1/4 inch. This prevents smoking, ensures an even burn, and extends the life of your candle.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="care-step">
        <div class="care-step-num">02</div>
        <h4>Let it pool</h4>
        <p>On the first burn, let the wax melt all the way to the edge — about 2 hours for the 8 oz, 3 hours for the 13 oz. This creates a "memory" that prevents tunneling.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="care-step">
        <div class="care-step-num">03</div>
        <h4>Never burn past 4 hours</h4>
        <p>Burning too long overheats the vessel and degrades the fragrance. Four hours max per session. Snuff, don't blow, to preserve the scent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:64px">
      <h2>Safety</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Never leave a burning candle unattended.</li>
        <li>Keep away from drafts, children, and pets.</li>
        <li>Burn on a stable, heat-resistant surface.</li>
        <li>Stop burning when 1/2 inch of wax remains.</li>
        <li>Don't burn the candle if the vessel is cracked or chipped.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:64px">
      <h2>Cleaning & refilling</h2>
      <p>When your candle is done, place the vessel in the freezer for 30 minutes. The remaining wax will contract and pop out easily. Wipe the inside with a paper towel, then wash with warm soapy water.</p>
      <p>Once clean, your vessel becomes a cup, a planter, a catch-all, or — if you join our refill program — a brand new candle at 30% off.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:64px">
      <h2>Diffuser care</h2>
      <p>Flip the reeds every 1–2 weeks to refresh the scent. If the scent fades, add a few drops of our Aroma Oil Refill. Replace reeds every 3–4 months, or when they become saturated and stop drawing oil effectively.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

